  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I couldn't build with `vite build` or run it in a browser, so none of it has been checked visually. Two risks: the follow camera's offset convention and the default shadow extents were read from engine source, not seen on screen.\n\n- **Bird:** it is built from primitives only. The body is an ellipsoid, the head a sphere, the beak a cone, and the eyes two small spheres. The tail has 5 fanned feather boxes. Each wing has a shoulder joint, an inner box, an elbow joint, and an outer box plus a tip box.\n- **Flight:** it circles at radius 6 and height 4, with the heading set to the tangent. A constant bank of about 0.38 rad tilts it toward the centre.\n- **Flap:** wings flap at 2 Hz. The outer segments lag the inner ones by 0.8 rad. The body bobs by 0.12 units with each flap.\n- **Loop:** time wraps every 8 s, which is exactly 16 flaps and one lap, so there is no jump.\n- **Scene:** a ground disc, 14 cone-on-trunk trees made with `instances` (2 near the centre, the rest outside the flight circle), a sky-coloured background with light fog, a hemisphere light, and one shadow-casting directional light.\n- **Camera:** it uses `camera.follow` with `targetNode: \"bird\"`. Its offset is [8, 3.5, -5] in the bird's own frame, so it stays outside the circle, above and slightly behind the bird, and looks at it.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()`.\n\n",
